Article 30
(1) Every person may participate in the implementation of Women's Protection in the Region. (2) Participation as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out by individuals, groups as well as - 34 - social community organizations, non-governmental organizations, educational institutions, Law Enforcement Institutions, service institutions, religious institutions, Islamic boarding schools, professional organizations, legal aid organizations, youth organizations, broadcasting supervisory institutions, media, communities, professional institutions, business entities and other related stakeholders.
(3) Participation as referred to in paragraph (1) may take the form of:
a. providing information or reporting to the competent authority if aware of acts of violence, and or exploitation and or discrimination against women;
